{"id":"resp_abb6d2ba08acc59f","created_at":1795591097,"incomplete_details":null,"instructions":null,"metadata":null,"model":"gpt-oss-120b","object":"response","output":[{"id":"rs_94472ebe48237e5e","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","content":[{"text":"We need to repair the previous candidate Turtle SHACL. The parse error is due to \"Prefix ':' not bound\". In Turtle, using ':CategoryAShipShape' requires a base prefix ':' bound via @base or a prefix definition like @prefix : <...>. Usually we can define a base prefix by adding @base <...> . but often we bind ':' to a default namespace. The rest of prefixes are defined as sh:, rdf:, etc. Need to add a prefix for ':' maybe to the same namespace as the shape, e.g., <https://example.org/shapes#> or similar. Since not specified, we can use a placeholder like <https://example.org/shapes#>. Must preserve everything else.\n\nAlso need to ensure syntax is correct: need a period after each shape definition? Already ends with '.' after closing bracket. Also need to ensure there is a space before the '.'? It ends with ']' . ; Actually shape block ends with '] .' The closing of shape: sh:property [ ... ] ; sh:property [ ... ] . That's fine.\n\nAdd prefix ':' mapping.\n\nLet's construct revised Turtle:\n\n@prefix : <https://example.org/shapes#> .\n\nBut we must ensure no parse error elsewhere. Check comments: \"# Ship must be assigned the Category A value\". Fine.\n\nAlso need prefix for nltl: but it's defined as @prefix nltl: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#> . That's present.\n\nThus final block includes all prefixes plus added ':'.\n\nReturn inside <BEGIN_SHACL> ... <END_SHACL>.\n\n","type":"reasoning_text"}],"encrypted_content":null,"status":null},{"id":"msg_91f4cbdb30315692","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"<BEGIN_SHACL>\n@prefix : <https://example.org/shapes#> .\n@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .\n@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .\n@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .\n@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .\n@prefix nltl: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#> .\n\n# Shape representing the regulatory definition of a Category A ship\n# Source: IMO‑001 “2.1 Category A ship means a ship designed for operation in polar waters in at least medium first‑year ice, which may include old ice inclusions.”\n# The admission declares the complete synthetic population of nltl:ship instances.\n\n:CategoryAShipShape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:targetClass nltl:ship ;\n    rdfs:label \"Category A ship shape\" ;\n    rdfs:comment \"Enforces that a ship classified as Category A has the required design ice condition per IMO‑001 §2.1.\" ;\n    \n    # Ship must be assigned the Category A value\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path nltl:shipCategory ;\n        sh:hasValue nltl:polarShipCategoryA ;\n        sh:severity sh:Info ;\n        sh:message \"Ship is classified as Category A (polarShipCategoryA).\" ;\n    ] ;\n    \n    # Design ice condition must be at least medium first‑year ice with possible old‑ice inclusions\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path nltl:designIceCondition ;\n        sh:hasValue nltl:mediumFirstYearIceWithPossibleOldIceInclusions ;\n        sh:severity sh:Violation ;\n        sh:message \"Category A ship must be designed for operation in at least medium first‑year ice (may include old ice inclusions).\" ;\n    ] .\n<END_SHACL>","type":"output_text","logprobs":null}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":null}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"temperature":1.0,"tool_choice":"none","tools":[],"top_p":1.0,"background":false,"max_output_tokens":16000,"max_tool_calls":null,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt":null,"prompt_cache_options":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":null,"reasoning":null,"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"auto","status":"completed","text":null,"top_logprobs":null,"truncation":"disabled","usage":{"input_tokens":30626,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":64,"cache_